I've modified https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/83459 so that `getAssetInfo` can optionally read `SparePartNumber` (via an arg).

```

inline void extractAssetInfo(
    const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
    const nlohmann::json::json_pointer& jsonKeyName,
    const dbus::utility::DBusPropertiesMap& assetList,
    bool includeSparePartNumber = false);

inline void getAssetInfo(const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,
                         const std::string& serviceName,
                         const std::string& dbusPath,
                         const nlohmann::json::json_pointer& jsonKeyName,
                         bool includeSparePartNumber = false);
```

The caller already checks the existence of the interface - 
```
        if (interface == "xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.Asset")
        {
            asset_utils::getAssetInfo(...)
        }
```

So, I think dbus callback can handle `ec` as like how it is done like others.
In addition, `getAssetInfo` also handles the interface existence again...

I think it should be good if the other dbus error would return internalError.
```
            if (ec)
            {
                if (ec.value() != EBADR)
                {
                    BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR("DBUS response error for Properties {}",
                                     ec.value());
                    messages::internalError(asyncResp->res);
                }
                return; <-- No interface
            }
```

The utility function `getAssetInfo()` checks the existence of interface, and it does no-op if so.

If the interface exists but it has a dbus-error, it will return an error.
(I think this would be as how it needs to be handled for dbus call).

```
            if (ec)
            {
                if (ec.value() != EBADR)
                {
                    BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR("DBUS response error for Properties {}",
                                     ec.value());
                    messages::internalError(asyncResp->res);
                }
                return; <-- No interface
            }
```
